# The linked `mpn_mul_basecase_rt` object as a literal

The Lean fork (spitters/lean4, branch `catcrypt-mpn-4.36.0` at `bd336156`) links
`src/runtime/catcrypt/mpn_mul_basecase_rt_owned.o` (1400 bytes, SHA-256
`3904b98a72300d7170466cbf96f1ac677cc8a338c70d53ed8959b760b18a7f90`). The object emitted at the
current base by `MpnRuntimeBytesEmit.emitTo` differs from it (SHA-256 `d3c8ec1d…`), so the
theorems about the linked multiply are stated about the bytes of the linked object, given here
as a literal (`mulObj`, the file's bytes in order).

## Main results

* `mulObj_eq`: the object is the single-leaf ELF object of the encoder's wrapper
  (`ElfObject.buildElfObjectMulti`) around the 751 function bytes `mulText`, defining the
  symbol `mpn_mul_basecase_rt`.
* `mulText_decode`: those bytes decode to the program `mulDec`: prologue, a do-while outer
  loop whose trip holds a do-while inner loop, epilogue (`mulPre`, `mulOHead`, `mulInner`,
  `mulOTail`, `mulPost`).
